(an integrable representative, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"ec5f34b0092e1daf\" href=\"?note=ec5f34b0092e1daf\" title=\"58-df-L1\">58-df-L1</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\alpha \\in \\mathbb{R}_{&gt;0}\">\\(\\alpha \\in \\mathbb{R}_{&gt;0}\\)</span> (positive threshold)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{ProbabilityMeasure}_S(\\mu,X,\\Sigma)\">\\(\\operatorname{ProbabilityMeasure}_S(\\mu,X,\\Sigma)\\)</span> (probability-measure predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"0578a357a86e9d8f\" href=\"?note=0578a357a86e9d8f\" title=\"58-df-probability-space\">58-df-probability-space</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{InvariantMeasure}_S(\\mu,T;X,\\Sigma)\">\\(\\mathrm{InvariantMeasure}_S(\\mu,T;X,\\Sigma)\\)</span> (invariant-measure predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"56239458358186f6\" href=\"?note=56239458358186f6\" title=\"58-df-invariant-measure\">58-df-invariant-measure</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{cor\\text{-}maximal\\text{-}inequality} \\vdash \\Bigl(\\operatorname{ProbabilityMeasure}_S(\\mu,X,\\Sigma)\\land\\mathrm{InvariantMeasure}_S(\\mu,T;X,\\Sigma)\\land\\mathrm{IntegrableFunction}_S(f;X,\\Sigma,\\mu)\\land\\alpha&gt;0\\Bigr)\\to\\mu\\!\\left(\\left\\{x\\in X:\\sup_{n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}}\\left|\\frac1n\\sum_{i=0}^{n-1}f(T^i(x))\\right|&gt;\\alpha\\right\\}\\right)\\leq\\frac1\\alpha\\int_X|f|\\,d\\mu\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{cor\\text{-}maximal\\text{-}inequality} \\vdash \\Bigl(\\operatorname{ProbabilityMeasure}_S(\\mu,X,\\Sigma)\\land\\mathrm{InvariantMeasure}_S(\\mu,T;X,\\Sigma)\\land\\mathrm{IntegrableFunction}_S(f;X,\\Sigma,\\mu)\\land\\alpha&gt;0\\Bigr)\\to\\mu\\!\\left(\\left\\{x\\in X:\\sup_{n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}}\\left|\\frac1n\\sum_{i=0}^{n-1}f(T^i(x))\\right|&gt;\\alpha\\right\\}\\right)\\leq\\frac1\\alpha\\int_X|f|\\,d\\mu\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>This is the weak <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(1,1)\">\\((1,1)\\)</span> maximal inequality for ergodic averages. Replacing averages by unnormalised partial sums would make the displayed bound false.</li>\n<li>The statement uses an integrable representative rather than applying pointwise operations to an <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L^1\">\\(L^1\\)</span> equivalence class.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-probability-space","status":"resolved","id":"0578a357a86e9d8f","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-probability-space]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-invariant-measure","status":"resolved","id":"56239458358186f6","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-invariant-measure]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-L1","status":"resolved","id":"ec5f34b0092e1daf","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-L1]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-L1","status":"resolved","id":"ec5f34b0092e1daf","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{IntegrableFunction}_S(f;X,\\Sigma,\\mu)$ (an integrable representative, see [[58-df-L1]])","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-probability-space","status":"resolved","id":"0578a357a86e9d8f","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\operatorname{ProbabilityMeasure}_S(\\mu,X,\\Sigma)$ (probability-measure predicate, see [[58-df-probability-space]])","embed":false},{"targe